    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Cardlytics is navigating a transition marked by shrinking scale paired with improving margins, reflecting a shift toward higher-quality revenue. Recent reports highlight new data monetization efforts and incremental progress in the U.K. business, though advertiser retention is mixed—new and returning advertisers are partly offset by some switching to competing platforms. The dramatic collapse in short interest suggests extreme bearish positioning has unwound, tempering the negative sentiment that previously surrounded the stock.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership adopted a cautious but constructive tone on the Q1 call, emphasizing margin discipline over top-line growth. The focus appears to be on pruning unprofitable activity, launching data-sales initiatives, and stabilizing the advertiser base. The market’s reception remains guarded—analysts maintain a hold rating and a low price target—but the sharp short-squeeze dynamic implies that execution on profitability is gradually restoring some credibility.",
